    {"claim_id": "C11", "claim": "Strict liability outperforms negligence under one specifiable condition: where harm is irreversible and post-hoc attribution is feasible, and the reasonable-developer test has nothing to measure against because no Hand-formula benchmark exists for emergent AI behavior.", "claimant": "safetyist", "type": "normative", "supported_by": [{"claim_id": "C11s", "scheme": "argument_from_precedent", "warrant": "Ultrahazardous-activity and defective-product liability already attach without proof of care precisely where no standard of care has crystallized."}], "attacked_by": [
